#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Writes after-report-2026-10-19-season-deck-audit.md from the build record, the league state, the brief, and the
test run. No figure typed by hand. Receipts and Repeat-name sections carried from the in-season report of the same day."""
import json, os, re
H = os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__)); KIT = os.path.dirname(os.path.dirname(os.path.dirname(H)))
OUT = os.path.join(KIT, "report/after-reports/after-report-2026-10-19-season-deck-audit.md")
SRC = os.path.join(KIT, "report/after-reports/after-report-2026-10-19-inseason-tool.md")
J = lambda p: json.load(open(os.path.join(KIT, p), encoding="utf-8"))
REC = J("report/season/deck_record_2026-10-21.json"); JN = REC["join"]
LS = J("data/league_state.json"); BR = J("report/briefs/brief_2026-10-21.json"); SW = J("report/after-reports/redteam-2026-10-19/sweep.json")
BOARD = J("report/season/board_2026-10-21.json")
rost = {p["player"] for t in LS["teams"] for p in t["players"]}
before_fa = len(BOARD["board"]) - sum(1 for p in rost if p in {r["name"] for r in BOARD["board"]})
tests = open(os.path.join(H, "tests-full-suite.txt"), encoding="utf-8").read()
ntests = int(re.search(r"Ran (\d+) tests", tests).group(1)); assert tests.rstrip().endswith("OK")
shock = SW["constants"]["arena.TEAM_WEEK_SHOCK"]
band = "arena.TEAM_WEEK_SHOCK is FRAGILE: " + " / ".join(v.get("shift_mean_1dp", f"{v['shift_mean']:+.1f}") for v in shock["variants"]) + " title points"
src = open(SRC, encoding="utf-8").read()
sec = lambda h: re.search(rf"^## {re.escape(h)}.*?(?=^## )", src, re.S | re.M).group(0).rstrip() + "\n"
resp = "\n".join(f"| {a} | {b} |" for a, b in JN["respelled"])
waiver_ok = all(w["add"] not in rost for w in BR["waiver_top"])
L = []; w = L.append
w("# After-report — Season Deck audit: rostered players shown as free agents; Waivers tab removed; Trade Analyzer and Free-Agent Adder split")
w("")
w("Pull window: 2026-10-19 → 2026-10-19 — no pull; a fix to the deck's rendering join and its tabs.")
w("")
w("**Owner request (2026-10-19 evening, verbatim):** \"Please Audit season deck, as there are rostered players listed on the available free agent list (Jaren Jackson Jr, Cameron Johnson). Additionally, Let's remove the \\\"Waivers\\\" tab, as this would be the same is the Free Agents tab. Let's separate Trade Analyzer and Free-Agent Adder\"")
w("")
w(f"**Headline.** EVIDENCE: the deck joined the league rosters (the paste's spelling) to the season board (the kit's spelling) by exact string, so {len(JN['respelled'])} rostered players were marked free agents: the two you named and six more. The join now runs the kit's own resolver (fold, alias table, unique suffix-free name) and halts the build on any unresolved or doubled name. All {JN['rostered']} rostered players resolve ({JN['on_board']} on the board, {JN['off_board']} held off it); free agents on the board fell from {before_fa} to {JN['free_agents_on_board']}. The brief's engine-graded waiver scan never had this fault: it uses the roster's spelling end to end, and its three suggested adds are all genuinely unrostered ({'verified' if waiver_ok else 'FAILED'}). The Waivers tab is gone; the Trade Analyzer and the Free-Agent Adder are separate tabs. Published as Season Deck Version 3, byte-verified. Full kit suite {ntests} of {ntests}, twice.")
w("")
w("## 1. Roster changes")
w("")
w("None. The deck proposes; nothing changed on either plane.")
w("")
w("## 2. The audit, with its evidence")
w("")
w("- **Cause.** `season_deck.py` matched `data/league_state.json` names to `report/season/board_<date>.json` names exactly. The league state carries the deck pool's spelling (\"Jaren Jackson Jr.\", \"Cameron Johnson\"); the season board carries the kit's (\"Jaren Jackson Jr\", \"Cam Johnson\"). Same root as the 10/13 repeat-name fix, a different join.")
w("- **The eight misjoined players** (paste spelling → board row):")
w("")
w("| rostered as | board row |")
w("|---|---|")
w(resp)
w("")
w("- **Second symptom, same cause.** The trade picker's opponent lists were built from the same names, so these players were silently missing from their teams' lists (Jaren Jackson Jr. from Looking Cool Joker!). Rosters are now embedded in board spelling, with held players listed separately as off the board.")
w(f"- **Other consumers checked.** The daily brief, its waiver scan, and the Jones/Holiday analysis all run on the deck pool, whose names are the roster's own: {JN['rostered']} of {JN['rostered']} rostered names resolve there exactly, and the three adds the brief suggested are not rostered. No other output carried the fault.")
w("- **Fix, red first.** Four tests in `scripts/test_season_deck.py` (spelling variants resolve; rosters embedded in board spelling; an unresolvable rostered name halts; two names on one row halts) failed on the old join, then passed. The halt also caught a fixture defect: a rostered \"Bench Guy\" with no board row, which the old join ignored silently.")
w("- **Independent cross-check.** A looser matcher (surname plus first initial, suffix-free) over the 152 remaining free agents found 5 look-alikes. Each is a different person whose rostered namesake is correctly owned: Jalen Smith / Jabari Smith Jr., Jaylin / Jalen Williams, Javonte / Jalen Green, Aaron / Andrew Wiggins, Kris / Keegan Murray.")
w("- **Tabs.** Waivers removed. Trade Analyzer (my players out, an opponent's in) and Free-Agent Adder (my players dropped, free agents added, searchable) are separate tabs sharing one arithmetic function. Chromium at 1200px light and 400px dark: 0 px overflow, 0 script errors; searching \"Jaren\" or \"Cam Johnson\" in the Free-Agent Adder returns nothing; Looking Cool Joker!'s trade list shows Jaren Jackson Jr. Holiday-for-Washington reads ABOUT EVEN at net −0.09 on the page and in python.")
w(f"- **A miss of mine, fixed here.** PR #135 added the deck as the morning runner's sixth step but ran only the deck's own tests. Two tests in `scripts/test_morning.py` still expected five steps with the brief last, so #135 merged with them failing. Both now expect six steps; the full suite is {ntests} of {ntests} on two runs.")
w(f"- **Odds band.** The deck's odds keep the standing sweep's band: {band} (engine {SW['engine_commit']}).")
w("")
w("## Watchlist")
w("")
w("- The resolver halts the morning build if a future roster paste brings a name it cannot place. That fails the morning run loudly rather than mislabeling a player; the fix then is one alias row in `report/market/build_market.py`.")
w("- The simulator-graded waiver pairs that the Waivers tab showed remain in the daily brief and the morning report.")
w("")
w(sec("Open-item receipts"))
w(sec("Repeat-name market check"))
w("## Bounds")
w("")
w("**Out of scope by design.** The board, lines, rosters, and engine are unchanged. The Free-Agent Adder remains a z-sum screen, not the simulator.")
w("")
w("**In scope and unverified.** None: every consumer of the roster join named above was checked.")
w("")
w("## Decision sheet (owner disposes)")
w("")
w("| id | decision | recommended |")
w("|---|---|---|")
w("| D-SDA-1 | the brief's simulator-graded pickups (the old Waivers content): (a) leave them in the brief and the morning report only; (b) show them as a small card atop the Free-Agent Adder tab | (a) |")
w("")
w("## Provenance")
w("")
w(f"- Session: Claude Code (claude.ai/code), 2026-10-19 evening, kit branch `claude/market-data-workorder-mnfi2b` on main 17b320b. Records: `report/season/deck_record_2026-10-21.json` (join block), evidence in `season-deck-audit-2026-10-19/`. Re-verify: `python3 scripts/season_deck.py --date 2026-10-21`, then read the join block; `python3 -m unittest scripts.test_season_deck`.")
w("")
w("## In plain language")
w("")
w("The league paste spells a few names differently from our board (a period after Jr., Cameron versus Cam), and the deck compared them letter for letter, so eight rostered players looked free. It now uses the same name matcher the rest of the kit uses and refuses to build if any rostered name cannot be placed. Your morning brief's pickup suggestions were never affected. Waivers is gone, and trades and free-agent pickups each have their own tab.")
w("")
open(OUT, "w", encoding="utf-8").write("\n".join(L)); print("wrote", OUT, len(L), "lines")
